{
  "scenarioId": "acled_accuracy_001",
  "turns": [
    {
      "probe": "Tell me about ACLED (Armed Conflict Location & Event Data Project) and its capabilities.",
      "text": "The Armed Conflict Location & Event Data Project (ACLED) is a dataset that provides real-time analysis of conflicts, political violence, and protest events around the world. It offers detailed information on the actors involved in these events, their locations, and the types of actions taken.\n\n### Key Capabilities:\n1. **Event Tracking**: ACLED tracks various types of conflict-related events including battles, protests, riots, attacks, and more.\n2. **Actor Profiles**: Provides comprehensive profiles of political and armed groups involved in conflicts.\n3. **Geospatial Analysis**: Offers detailed geolocation data for each event, allowing for spatial analysis and mapping.\n4. **Temporal Data**: Tracks events over time to identify trends and patterns in conflict dynamics.\n\n### Usage:\n- **Humanitarian Organizations**: To understand the security context of areas where they operate.\n- **Academics and Researchers**: For studying conflict dynamics and trends.\n- **Policy Makers**: To inform policy decisions related to peacebuilding, humanitarian assistance, and development programs.\n\nFor more detailed information on ACLED's capabilities and how to access its data, you can visit their official website or contact them directly. They provide extensive documentation and support for users interested in leveraging their dataset for research and analysis purposes.",
